sity of Rhode Island","years":[1990]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210114556","name":"First Institute of Oceanography","years":[1989]}],"author_id":"A5104385630","ca_plastic_works_count":1,"ca_works_count":1,"citations_by_year":[{"all":1998,"plastic":0,"year":2017},{"all":2275,"plastic":0,"year":2018},{"all":2405,"plastic":0,"year":2019},{"all":3023,"plastic":0,"year":2020},{"all":3550,"plastic":0,"year":2021},{"all":3882,"plastic":0,"year":2022},{"all":4423,"plastic":0,"year":2023},{"all":4168,"plastic":0,"year":2024},{"all":4043,"plastic":0,"year":2025},{"all":3424,"plastic":2,"year":2026}],"cited_by_count":48011,"domain_tags":[],"early_career":false,"first_pub_year":1981,"first_year":2026,"h_index":106,"institution_ids":["I150209017"],"last_year":2026,"m_quotient":2.36,"name":"Lisa Ann Levin","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2858-8622","plastic_basis":"openalex","plastic_citations":2,"plastic_works_count":1,"primary_affiliations":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I150209017","name":"Scripps Institution of Oceanography","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I36258959","name":"University of California San Diego","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":null,"rising_score":null,"work_count":1,"work_ids":["W7166866676"]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"The seafloor is recognized as a major sink for marine debris, while deep-sea litter remains poorly investigated due to the logistical and economic constraints associated with seabed exploration. This study reports for the first time the occurrence of marine debris found on the Argentine deep seafloor using the SOI\u2019s Remotely Operated Vehicle (ROV), providing the first documented evidence for this region. A total of 29 litter items were recorded across 55.6 km of surveyed seafloor. The highest debris abundance was recorded in submarine canyon areas (1.4 items/km), whereas the Malvinas Basin showed the lowest levels (0.1 items/km), likely associated with hydrodynamic conditions. In addition, plastic items, fishing ropes, and nets were the most frequently recorded types of debris. These findings establish a baseline of the current status of deep-sea marine debris and propose future directions for the region.","author_count":26,"author_ids":["A5001212008","A5014926435","A5015081236","A5031963947","A5035062626","A5049320933","A5051760363","A5055709989","A5060331908","A5080396124","A5088303238","A5093584919","A5104385630","A5108983158","A5111097397","A5119454986","A5121263423","A5137015781","A5139726586","A5139751870","A5139759529","A5139761135","A5139776817","A5139778560","A5139783821","A5139851585"],"author_institution_ids":["I150209017"],"authors":[{"id":"A5060331908","name":"M.G. Ardusso"},{"id":"A5139751870","name":"Florencia B. Rial"},{"id":"A5049320933","name":"Melisa Daiana Fern\u00e1ndez-Severini"},{"id":"A5121263423","name":"Ele Beruschi"},{"id":"A5111097397","name":"Luana Acosta"},{"id":"A5108983158","name":"Andrea Natalia Alvarez"},{"id":"A5035062626","name":"Juan Cruz Carbajal"},{"id":"A5139776817","name":"Danya Awshah"},{"id":"A5139783821","name":"Xenia Barnes"},{"id":"A5139726586","name":"Lucia Chesta"},{"id":"A5031963947","name":"Moira R. D\u00e9cima"},{"id":"A5015081236","name":"Brenda L. Doti"},{"id":"A5088303238","name":"Juliana Gim\u00e9nez"},{"id":"A5014926435","name":"J.I. Isola"},{"id":"A5080396124","name":"Daniel M. Lauretta"},{"id":"A5104385630","name":"Lisa Ann Levin"},{"id":"A5139851585","name":"Lucia Mart\u00ednez Alzaga"},{"id":"A5139778560","name":"Siara Mitchel"},{"id":"A5137015781","name":"Leonel Pacheco"},{"id":"A5055709989","name":"Fabrizio Scarabino"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":2,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmars.2026.1876155","domain_tags":["occurrence_and_monitoring"],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I150209017","I151201029","I180910786","I186143895","I24354313","I4210086432","I4210125789","I4387156258","I4405253718","I4405284269","I56858762","I84392919"],"is_